WEBVTT

00:00.550 --> 00:02.740
Here's your pay for June.

00:02.690 --> 00:05.100
<b></b>Tsukishima Riho

00:03.320 --> 00:05.100
Good work this month.

00:05.100 --> 00:08.260
All right!

00:09.610 --> 00:14.490
Now, I have an important 
announcement for... you...

00:14.490 --> 00:17.770
Hey, Riho-chan, let's go buy summer clothes!

00:17.420 --> 00:19.240
Yay!

00:17.770 --> 00:20.450
Good idea. The sales should be on by now.

00:20.450 --> 00:23.980
Hey, wanna try out the new 
sweets shop by the station?

00:23.980 --> 00:25.250
Sounds good!

00:25.250 --> 00:27.770
I'm gonna buy new dumbbells!

00:27.770 --> 00:29.880
Do you really need more dumbbells?

00:30.170 --> 00:33.380
I envy you. Student life must be fun.

00:33.760 --> 00:36.390
If I'd sold this house 
and gone off to college,

00:36.390 --> 00:39.510
I'd be enjoying my own campus life right now.

00:39.510 --> 00:41.930
Don't talk about that 
like you could actually do it,

00:41.930 --> 00:43.500
you Grandma's boy.

00:44.510 --> 00:46.270
Who are you calling a Grandma's boy?!

00:46.270 --> 00:50.650
What exactly was the "campus life" 
you were envisioning, anyway?

00:50.650 --> 00:52.780
Were you hoping you'd get a girlfriend?

00:52.780 --> 00:53.650
Huh?

00:53.650 --> 00:56.960
You don't have to go to college for that.

00:56.960 --> 00:59.200
You've got five cute girlfriend candidates...

00:59.200 --> 01:01.410
right here!

01:01.410 --> 01:04.680
Why do I have to choose one of you?

01:04.680 --> 01:08.100
What makes you think 
you have the right to choose?

01:08.790 --> 01:12.180
Anyway, more importantly, 
I wanted to tell you guys...

01:13.440 --> 01:15.220
Here you go.

01:16.030 --> 01:20.010
It's summer now, 
so you'd prefer iced coffee, right?

01:20.010 --> 01:23.550
Oh, thanks. What brought this on, though?

01:23.550 --> 01:24.770
What do you mean?

01:24.770 --> 01:27.000
You said yourself...

01:27.000 --> 01:29.980
that you want to drink my coffee 
for the rest of your life.

01:31.420 --> 01:33.440
Don't phrase it in misleading ways.

01:33.440 --> 01:36.300
All I said was that you make good coffee.

01:36.300 --> 01:38.240
I never said "for the rest of my life."

01:39.510 --> 01:42.620
I was just kidding. 
I made enough for everyone.

01:42.620 --> 01:44.080
Jeez...

01:44.080 --> 01:47.620
You gotta stop springing these jokes 
on us out of nowhere.

01:48.610 --> 01:50.380
Anyway, Hayato-kun...

01:50.380 --> 01:52.980
You were about to tell us something?

01:56.080 --> 01:58.430
Summer is now beginning in earnest.

01:58.430 --> 02:03.510
Would you not like to work through 
summer break and make lots of money?

02:03.840 --> 02:05.440
What happened to you?

02:05.440 --> 02:07.270
You're kinda scaring me.

02:07.700 --> 02:10.350
Yes. I want to work.

02:10.350 --> 02:11.770
Stop that.

02:12.080 --> 02:14.890
Is there something you've 
been struggling to tell us?

02:14.890 --> 02:17.400
If it's something you decided on, 
we'll go along with it.

02:17.400 --> 02:18.760
Just tell us.

02:20.690 --> 02:23.080
I want to open a beach hut!

02:23.080 --> 02:27.770
So other than the Obon Festival, 
there'll be no summer break this year!

02:45.060 --> 02:47.640
<b></b>The Café Terrace and Its Goddesses

03:59.590 --> 04:02.720
<b>Episode 8: "A Beach Hut!"</b>

03:59.620 --> 04:02.720
<b>Episode 8: "A Beach Hut!"</b>

03:59.660 --> 04:02.720
<b>Episode 8: "A Beach Hut!"</b>

03:59.690 --> 04:02.720
<b>Episode 8: "A Beach Hut!"</b>

03:59.730 --> 04:02.720
<b>Episode 8: "A Beach Hut!"</b>

03:59.760 --> 04:02.720
<b>Episode 8: "A Beach Hut!"</b>

03:59.800 --> 04:02.720
<b>Episode 8: "A Beach Hut!"</b>

03:59.840 --> 04:02.720
<b>Episode 8: "A Beach Hut!"</b>

03:59.870 --> 04:02.720
<b>Episode 8: "A Beach Hut!"</b>

03:59.910 --> 04:02.720
<b>Episode 8: "A Beach Hut!"</b>

03:59.940 --> 04:02.720
<b>Episode 8: "A Beach Hut!"</b>

03:59.980 --> 04:02.720
<b>Episode 8: "A Beach Hut!"</b>

04:00.010 --> 04:02.720
<b>Episode 8: "A Beach Hut!"</b>

04:00.050 --> 04:02.720
<b>Episode 8: "A Beach Hut!"</b>

04:00.090 --> 04:02.720
<b>Episode 8: "A Beach Hut!"</b>

04:00.120 --> 04:02.720
<b>Episode 8: "A Beach Hut!"</b>

04:00.160 --> 04:02.720
<b>Episode 8: "A Beach Hut!"</b>

04:00.190 --> 04:02.720
<b>Episode 8: "A Beach Hut!"</b>

04:00.230 --> 04:02.720
<b>Episode 8: "A Beach Hut!"</b>

04:00.260 --> 04:02.720
<b>Episode 8: "A Beach Hut!"</b>

04:00.300 --> 04:02.720
<b>Episode 8: "A Beach Hut!"</b>

04:00.930 --> 04:02.720
I really am sorry

04:03.160 --> 04:05.400
for talking about quitting 
and all that dumb stuff.

04:06.160 --> 04:07.930
No, it's okay!

04:08.330 --> 04:11.430
We're the ones who should be sorry 
for not taking you seriously!

04:11.800 --> 04:12.520
Huh?

04:12.520 --> 04:16.560
We never realized you had 
such a thing for mustaches!

04:16.560 --> 04:18.140
We can go with...

04:18.140 --> 04:20.740
...Mussy Mustache Girls for the band name!

04:21.960 --> 04:25.070
Uh, I don't actually care 
about that anymore...

04:25.070 --> 04:27.450
It's okay! Let's start all over!

04:27.450 --> 04:29.120
Starting today...

04:29.120 --> 04:31.520
...we're Mussy Mustache Girls!

04:31.520 --> 04:33.460
I'm... really sorry.

04:35.010 --> 04:36.060
Now that I look,

04:36.060 --> 04:38.790
I guess they've already started 
setting up the beach hut.

04:38.790 --> 04:41.740
Not that I can see it from here, but...

04:41.740 --> 04:44.170
I did see a lot of heavy machinery out there.

04:44.620 --> 04:48.300
We do tend to get fewer customers in summer.

04:48.300 --> 04:52.720
So we're finally entering 
the beach hut battle!

04:52.720 --> 04:54.810
The beach hut <i>market</i>, Ami-chan.

04:54.810 --> 04:59.190
I'm glad the union gave us permission 
that easily, though.

04:59.190 --> 05:03.690
Yeah, they said the grandson of Familia's 
owner was more than welcome.

05:03.960 --> 05:06.320
So we have Grandma to thank again, huh?

05:06.320 --> 05:09.070
Yeah, and that comes 
with its own level of pressure.

05:09.070 --> 05:10.360
Hi-yah!

05:10.360 --> 05:13.520
If any tanned surfer dudes come by, 
I'll knock 'em out!

05:13.520 --> 05:15.960
Don't! There are good surfer dudes, too!

05:15.960 --> 05:17.080
Nope!

05:17.910 --> 05:21.380
Isn't it expensive to build 
a beach hut, though?

05:23.080 --> 05:26.920
I sank nearly four months' 
worth of revenue into it.

05:26.920 --> 05:27.800
What?!

05:29.670 --> 05:32.560
We're going all-in on this wager!

05:32.560 --> 05:36.280
Seriously? I have a bad feeling about this.

05:37.030 --> 05:38.190
Well...

05:38.190 --> 05:40.730
In that case, we'd better 
start promoting, huh?

05:40.730 --> 05:43.310
A grammable, summery menu,

05:43.310 --> 05:45.240
girls in cute uniforms...

05:45.530 --> 05:48.970
and nice, orthodox coffee made by the owner.

05:49.430 --> 05:50.590
Hey, uh...

05:51.450 --> 05:55.000
I was thinking about a watermelon 
parfait for our summer menu.

05:55.640 --> 05:57.000
What do you think?

05:57.000 --> 05:58.520
Sounds good.

05:58.520 --> 06:00.320
Yeah! Could be a hit!

06:00.320 --> 06:02.700
And I'll crack open the watermelon!

06:02.700 --> 06:04.250
Why do we need to crack it open?

06:04.670 --> 06:08.010
So we should probably 
overhaul our web page, too!

06:08.010 --> 06:09.710
I'll leave that to you.

06:09.710 --> 06:11.280
Just don't push yourself too hard.

06:11.280 --> 06:12.560
I won't!

06:12.560 --> 06:13.890
Captain!

06:13.890 --> 06:17.150
What are we going to call our beach hut?

06:17.150 --> 06:17.930
Hmm...

06:18.750 --> 06:21.980
That's a good question, Private Tsuruga.

06:21.980 --> 06:24.160
Familia Type 0...

06:22.150 --> 06:24.150
<b>Type 0</b>

06:24.150 --> 06:24.980
Kai!

06:24.150 --> 06:25.400
<b>Kai</b>

06:27.710 --> 06:30.700
Like an upgrade! That's so cool!

06:32.360 --> 06:35.470
This wouldn't have happened 
if you weren't goofing around!

06:35.470 --> 06:37.060
Sorry.

06:38.030 --> 06:40.420
I'll get something to wipe it up with.

06:40.420 --> 06:42.440
You don't want it to stain.

06:42.440 --> 06:46.760
I bet you two would get all wound up 
and break glasses if you tried karaoke!

06:47.800 --> 06:49.130
Hayato-kun!

06:51.090 --> 06:52.180
How's this?

06:53.030 --> 06:57.340
Since it's summer, 
I went for a hibiscus hair band.

06:57.850 --> 06:59.190
What do you think?

06:59.730 --> 07:02.230
What happened to you?

07:02.520 --> 07:05.420
Did the heat finally drive you insane?

07:06.230 --> 07:07.990
It's a costume for the beach hut!

07:08.330 --> 07:10.320
I made one for the occasion!

07:10.320 --> 07:13.070
O-Okay, I get it. Now put some clothes on!

07:13.070 --> 07:16.240
Also, I think one hibiscus is enough.

07:16.540 --> 07:18.920
Why are you being all shy? It's a swimsuit top.

07:18.920 --> 07:21.920
Why do <i>you</i> think the fact that 
it's a swimsuit top makes it okay?

07:22.360 --> 07:23.820
Ah...

07:23.820 --> 07:28.840
So you can't take it when girls are 
assertive about showing off to you, huh?

07:29.340 --> 07:33.640
Well, since it's a swimsuit top, 
I'm not embarrassed at all.

07:33.640 --> 07:34.600
Stop it!

07:34.600 --> 07:36.120
Are you a sadist?!

07:36.120 --> 07:41.400
Um, I'd be embarrassed, though. 
I'd prefer a T-shirt or something.

07:41.400 --> 07:42.170
Right?

07:42.960 --> 07:44.200
Riho-chan?

07:46.110 --> 07:47.700
Riho-chan?

07:50.180 --> 07:51.660
What got into her?

07:51.660 --> 07:54.200
You had to start goofing around, too.

07:54.200 --> 07:55.900
Must've pissed her off.

07:55.900 --> 07:57.580
Goofing around?!

07:57.580 --> 08:00.450
She's serious when it comes 
to this job, you know.

08:00.450 --> 08:02.720
You should probably apologize to her.

08:02.720 --> 08:06.080
I-I wasn't being facetious or anything...

08:09.740 --> 08:10.890
She's back.

08:12.760 --> 08:14.970
So this is what you meant, right?

08:14.970 --> 08:17.420
This works pretty well, 
doesn't it, Ouka-chan?

08:18.850 --> 08:21.910
Riho-chan, that's literally 
just a swimsuit...

08:21.910 --> 08:23.600
What do you think, Hayato-kun?

08:23.930 --> 08:26.100
Give it a really good look!

08:27.730 --> 08:30.730
What're you being all shy about? Ew!

08:30.730 --> 08:33.130
Cut it out! What are you trying to do?!

08:33.130 --> 08:34.840
Let's be serious about this.

08:34.840 --> 08:36.740
I'm hungry.

08:41.010 --> 08:43.910
Mussy Mustache Girls...

08:47.190 --> 08:49.160
Well, whatever.

08:49.670 --> 08:51.670
<b>Alcohol Disinfecting Wipes</b>

08:51.960 --> 08:54.880
I think this works great, too!

08:54.880 --> 08:58.430
Cut it out! How do you get 
drunk off of disinfecting wipes?!

08:58.430 --> 09:01.290
Shiragiku-san, that's a hair band!

09:01.290 --> 09:03.180
Ami-chan, do something!

09:03.970 --> 09:06.440
Please recharge.

09:06.440 --> 09:07.440
Oh, come on!

09:07.980 --> 09:10.160
Well, what do you think of my swimsuit?

09:10.160 --> 09:12.040
Look at it! Actually look!

09:12.040 --> 09:16.030
Okay, fine! Just do something 
about Shiragiku!

09:16.030 --> 09:17.990
What do you mean, "fine"?!

09:18.440 --> 09:20.740
Okay, okay. Yes, it's very cute.

09:21.240 --> 09:24.010
Your swimsuit is the cutest of all.

09:24.010 --> 09:25.000
Grr!

09:25.470 --> 09:27.710
Are you making fun of me?!

09:26.720 --> 09:29.630
Wh-What do you want me to say, then?!

09:29.960 --> 09:31.690
You guys, calm down!

09:31.690 --> 09:32.630
I'm back.

09:33.510 --> 09:36.240
Akane! Perfect timing!

09:36.240 --> 09:38.260
Do something about these guys!

09:38.800 --> 09:45.270
We changed our band name to 
Mussy Mustache Girls, like you suggested.

09:45.600 --> 09:46.330
Huh?

09:46.960 --> 09:48.650
Oh, you did?

09:49.250 --> 09:50.220
Later.

09:52.880 --> 09:54.780
Help me out here!

10:00.420 --> 10:03.540
I get it. When she said...

10:03.790 --> 10:07.910
My friend's band is thinking of 
changing their band name.

10:08.270 --> 10:11.920
So she was talking about her own band.

10:13.560 --> 10:15.670
Could it be that she actually...

10:16.060 --> 10:19.180
thinks of Hayato-kun as...

10:25.760 --> 10:29.940
Okay, what to do about everyone's shifts...

10:30.600 --> 10:33.770
Working at a beach hut isn't gonna be easy.

10:34.690 --> 10:37.820
I need to make sure 
they all get equal treatment.

10:39.400 --> 10:40.950
Oh, crap!

10:41.450 --> 10:43.720
I forgot I was in charge of dinner today!

10:43.720 --> 10:45.450
Food...

10:45.450 --> 10:48.910
<b>Ono Shiragiku's Gentle Awakening 2</b>

10:46.200 --> 10:49.750
<i>Ono Shiragiku's Gentle Awakening 2!</i>

10:50.200 --> 10:51.310
Mph...

10:52.250 --> 10:54.430
Aw, again?!

10:54.430 --> 10:57.770
Seriously, who keeps playing 
these pranks on me?!

10:59.270 --> 11:01.720
Come on, get moving!

11:01.720 --> 11:04.720
We need to take promotional photos!

11:04.720 --> 11:06.410
What the heck?

11:06.410 --> 11:10.250
At least let me take it easy for 
one last moment before we open.

11:10.250 --> 11:13.110
Don't talk like some old geezer!

11:13.480 --> 11:16.180
We gotta make a killing 
through the summer, too!

11:17.500 --> 11:18.780
What do you think?

11:18.780 --> 11:22.110
A new item for our beach hut menu: 
the watermelon parfait.

11:22.110 --> 11:26.140
Huh, you made it two colors 
by using yellow watermelons, too?

11:26.140 --> 11:28.370
It's gonna be our main draw for sure!

11:28.370 --> 11:31.600
It looks so good! Can I eat it?

11:31.600 --> 11:33.150
Like hell you can.

11:33.150 --> 11:35.620
You can eat it after 
we finish taking pictures.

11:36.630 --> 11:39.260
Make sure you get a good shot, Hayato-kun.

11:39.260 --> 11:42.410
Kiku-chan worked hard to put this together.

11:42.410 --> 11:43.800
I know.

11:44.520 --> 11:48.770
You might not think it, but I'm confident 
in my... photography...

11:49.200 --> 11:51.770
Wait, the angle of 
the whipped cream dollop...

11:52.740 --> 11:54.920
Hurry it up!

11:54.920 --> 11:58.430
There's that irritating 
Tokyo U perfectionism.

11:58.430 --> 12:01.400
That should do it.

12:02.780 --> 12:04.540
Don't bomb my photo!

12:04.540 --> 12:09.280
I thought people might like 
a hut with funny waitresses!

12:09.660 --> 12:11.840
Yummy!

12:11.840 --> 12:12.960
Don't eat that!

12:12.960 --> 12:15.040
Well, you got your pictures, didn't you?

12:15.040 --> 12:17.130
I only got one,

12:17.130 --> 12:19.800
and some weirdo jumped into it!

12:20.060 --> 12:22.920
Huh? Hurry up and take another, then.

12:22.920 --> 12:24.550
You've already eaten part of it!

12:24.550 --> 12:27.680
You people get in my way at every step!

12:27.680 --> 12:30.810
Shiragiku, sorry, but could you 
make another one?

12:30.810 --> 12:32.180
S-Sorry...

12:32.520 --> 12:34.830
I don't have any watermelon left.

12:34.830 --> 12:38.380
Are you serious? 
And I was all ready to do this...

12:41.030 --> 12:42.570
In that case...

12:45.080 --> 12:46.780
Okay, go ahead!

12:47.150 --> 12:49.530
You can start taking pictures!

12:49.530 --> 12:51.290
I'm so lost.

12:51.290 --> 12:54.330
Why do I have to take pictures of you guys?

12:54.660 --> 12:56.920
The weather's so nice today!

12:56.920 --> 13:01.030
Get some shots of us with an ocean 
backdrop for the web page!

13:01.550 --> 13:05.690
We might become popular 
as the café with the cute waitresses.

13:05.690 --> 13:07.300
Don't say that about yourself.

13:07.300 --> 13:09.470
Well, whatever.

13:09.470 --> 13:13.420
I just need to do as our chief 
of promotions says, right?

13:13.810 --> 13:16.810
Go ahead and pose however you want.

13:18.840 --> 13:20.570
Uh, I think...

13:20.570 --> 13:22.360
one of you is not like the others.

13:22.360 --> 13:23.990
You still okay with this?

13:25.960 --> 13:27.570
I mean you, Ami!

13:27.570 --> 13:28.470
Oh.

13:28.920 --> 13:30.750
I'm okay with it!

13:30.750 --> 13:32.080
Are you kidding me?!

13:32.410 --> 13:35.580
This is <i>my</i> business we're 
promoting here, you know.

13:35.580 --> 13:36.990
Oh, it's fine.

13:36.990 --> 13:40.440
Being the café with the funny waitress 
might make us popular.

13:40.440 --> 13:41.590
True.

13:41.590 --> 13:43.710
Which way do you want it, exactly?

13:43.710 --> 13:44.460
You people...

13:44.720 --> 13:47.220
Right. And now...

13:47.220 --> 13:48.990
Yeah. Time to head back.

13:48.990 --> 13:50.600
Wait... Ami-chan?

13:50.600 --> 13:52.600
You're not really gonna...

13:52.600 --> 13:54.430
Ocean!

13:54.430 --> 13:57.350
Wait, wait! Swimming season 
hasn't started yet!

13:57.630 --> 14:00.110
It's fine! I'll only go knee-deep!

14:00.110 --> 14:02.860
Don't blame me if your outfit gets wet!

14:02.860 --> 14:04.970
I bet that feels nice.

14:04.970 --> 14:06.860
Think we should join her?

14:16.580 --> 14:18.460
This feels great!

14:20.000 --> 14:22.700
Jeez, are they little kids or what?

14:23.640 --> 14:25.800
But since we're doing this...

14:26.380 --> 14:28.920
I guess I'll upload this, too.

14:30.610 --> 14:33.880
This really is exciting, though.

14:33.880 --> 14:35.780
Feels like summer's starting.

14:38.390 --> 14:39.900
<i>It Went Viral!</i>

14:38.390 --> 14:41.100
<b>It Went Viral!</b>

14:39.900 --> 14:41.100
I can't believe...

14:41.530 --> 14:44.460
it actually went viral.

14:46.580 --> 14:49.260
I was worried about 
how the first day would go,

14:49.680 --> 14:51.780
so I closed the café for the day

14:51.780 --> 14:54.840
and had all of our staff work here instead...

14:55.710 --> 14:57.000
Come on in!

14:57.000 --> 14:59.860
Welcome to Seaside Café Familia!

15:00.290 --> 15:01.640
Right this way.

15:01.640 --> 15:02.920
Thanks for waiting!

15:02.920 --> 15:03.720
Welcome.

15:03.720 --> 15:05.530
Please wait just a moment!

15:05.530 --> 15:07.050
Coming right up!

15:07.050 --> 15:09.300
A crowd like this on our first day...

15:09.680 --> 15:11.220
I made the right choice.

15:12.120 --> 15:13.220
Captain!

15:13.220 --> 15:14.300
What is it?

15:14.700 --> 15:20.560
Why is our beach hut's name not 
"Familia Type 0 Kai"?!

15:18.060 --> 15:20.560
<b>Type 0 Kai</b>

15:20.560 --> 15:24.780
Sorry. It was met with vehement opposition 
from the Naval General Staff,

15:24.780 --> 15:26.410
so we were forced to abandon it.

15:26.410 --> 15:27.940
Obviously.

15:27.940 --> 15:29.770
This isn't a game.

15:29.770 --> 15:31.040
Hey, look!

15:31.040 --> 15:34.450
More importantly, how do you like 
our new costumes?

15:34.720 --> 15:38.190
I remade them according to 
Shiragiku-san's specifications.

15:38.190 --> 15:39.580
Aren't they cute?

15:40.010 --> 15:43.830
I'd be embarrassed to wear a 
swimsuit top that exposes too much...

15:44.090 --> 15:47.460
This is just about right for me.

15:48.050 --> 15:49.570
Really?

15:49.570 --> 15:51.220
Yeah.

15:51.220 --> 15:52.380
<i>Twinkle.</i>

15:53.000 --> 15:54.550
Hey, Shiragiku-san...

15:55.330 --> 15:57.500
Didn't those disinfecting wipes 
the other day get you—

15:57.500 --> 15:58.330
Ami-chan.

15:58.850 --> 16:00.490
Hard at work, eh?

16:00.850 --> 16:03.500
I brought some guests 
in celebration of your opening here.

16:03.500 --> 16:05.690
Working hard, second generation?

16:05.690 --> 16:07.720
It's the wagashi lady!

16:07.720 --> 16:08.570
Hi, there.

16:08.570 --> 16:11.160
That's quite the swimsuit.

16:11.160 --> 16:12.700
Oh? Is it?

16:13.020 --> 16:17.120
When we were younger, this was 
the kind of thing everyone wore.

16:17.120 --> 16:20.120
You're still young, Acchan!

16:20.120 --> 16:22.060
You got a nice tush on ya!

16:22.060 --> 16:24.370
Don't stand there gawking!

16:24.370 --> 16:26.760
Go sit down and order, already!

16:26.760 --> 16:28.520
Y-Yes, ma'am!

16:29.880 --> 16:33.260
Your abs are so ripped! Can I touch 'em?

16:33.260 --> 16:35.610
Uh, sure...

16:35.610 --> 16:39.010
Ami-chan, let's go! There's work to do!

16:39.010 --> 16:41.610
Excuse me! Two watermelon parfaits, please.

16:41.610 --> 16:43.500
Can I get another iced coffee?

16:43.500 --> 16:44.640
Me, too!

16:44.640 --> 16:45.560
Coming!

16:45.560 --> 16:47.980
Oh, and add a toasted sandwich to that.

16:48.400 --> 16:49.690
Got another order.

16:51.160 --> 16:53.740
Looks like our first day 
was a big success, at least.

16:55.060 --> 16:57.080
You can take a break, Riho-chan.

16:57.080 --> 16:58.990
I'll take over on the floor.

16:58.990 --> 17:02.400
Nah, I'm fine. You should take a break.

17:02.400 --> 17:03.750
Excuse me!

17:03.750 --> 17:05.050
Coming!

17:06.040 --> 17:07.250
Riho-chan...

17:09.880 --> 17:11.500
Welcome!

17:13.480 --> 17:14.470
Hey!

17:14.760 --> 17:16.170
Where's my cola?

17:16.170 --> 17:19.470
Oh, I'm sorry. I'll bring it right out.

17:19.770 --> 17:22.740
Hayato-kun, a guy in the terrace seating...

17:23.480 --> 17:27.200
I see. So you can just make 
cold brew and store it.

17:27.200 --> 17:28.010
Yep.

17:30.500 --> 17:33.850
It takes too long to just grind 
more beans for every order.

17:35.030 --> 17:37.360
Excuse me! Just what are you two doing?

17:37.360 --> 17:40.200
We're busy here! Quit slacking off!

17:40.200 --> 17:43.500
And you, Akane-chan! 
Quit lazing around and clear the tables!

17:43.500 --> 17:47.500
Sorry about that. We got more 
iced coffee orders than I expected,

17:47.960 --> 17:50.860
so I was asking her 
how we could serve it faster.

17:51.770 --> 17:55.630
No, I'm sorry, Riho. 
This wasn't the time to talk.

17:56.120 --> 17:58.010
I'll go clear tables.

17:58.010 --> 18:00.680
If you know that, then get to work already!

18:00.680 --> 18:03.010
The dishes are piling up here!

18:03.010 --> 18:05.690
Hey, what are you so irritated about?

18:05.690 --> 18:07.640
Go take a break.

18:07.640 --> 18:09.270
I'll do that later!

18:16.320 --> 18:17.130
Riho!

18:17.130 --> 18:18.030
Hey!

18:18.520 --> 18:19.640
Are you okay?!

18:19.640 --> 18:22.780
I'm... perfectly fine.

18:23.600 --> 18:26.790
You're the one who needs 
to get your act together!

18:26.790 --> 18:30.790
We're this busy... and you're...

18:30.790 --> 18:34.380
chatting up... a waitress...

18:36.300 --> 18:37.770
Hey! Riho!

18:37.770 --> 18:39.030
Riho!

18:50.960 --> 18:52.180
Wait!

18:55.760 --> 18:58.430
Don't go!

19:05.670 --> 19:06.700
Huh?

19:07.240 --> 19:08.200
Morning.

19:10.770 --> 19:13.120
Huh?! Oh my gosh! Hayato-ku—

19:13.120 --> 19:16.330
Wait, why am I in my own room?

19:16.330 --> 19:18.800
Because you ignored everyone's advice.

19:18.800 --> 19:21.020
Mild heatstroke, they said.

19:21.020 --> 19:23.260
I had them check you out 
at the first aid station,

19:23.680 --> 19:27.400
but they said that if you lived close by, 
you should rest at home.

19:27.400 --> 19:30.520
Oh... So I passed out.

19:31.400 --> 19:32.520
Yeah.

19:32.520 --> 19:34.880
They said to drink water when you woke up.

19:34.880 --> 19:37.730
You know, I really wish 
you'd stop this already.

19:38.480 --> 19:41.570
You're right. Sorry.

19:42.210 --> 19:45.580
A part-timer who passes out 
on the beach hut's first day

19:46.010 --> 19:47.350
is just a nuisance, right?

19:49.330 --> 19:51.930
That doesn't even matter.

19:51.930 --> 19:53.330
H-Hey—

19:53.330 --> 19:58.090
I'm telling you not to work until 
you keel over. It's bad for my heart.

19:59.790 --> 20:03.090
Even I lost my cool a little bit, you know.

20:05.270 --> 20:07.950
You were that worried?

20:07.950 --> 20:09.600
Of course I was.

20:11.060 --> 20:12.650
About me?

20:12.650 --> 20:13.600
What did I say?

20:14.120 --> 20:15.370
Yes, about you.

20:16.390 --> 20:17.770
I see...

20:26.290 --> 20:27.510
I'm sorry.

20:28.200 --> 20:30.470
I'll be more careful.

20:31.650 --> 20:33.300
G-Good...

20:37.800 --> 20:40.630
Okay, just rest a little longer.

20:40.630 --> 20:42.490
Here, lie down.

20:42.490 --> 20:43.130
Okay.

20:44.320 --> 20:45.190
Hey...

20:46.790 --> 20:49.650
I had a scary dream earlier.

20:49.650 --> 20:52.520
Could you stay just a little bit longer?

20:54.040 --> 20:55.040
Sure.

20:56.100 --> 20:57.700
And...

20:59.520 --> 21:00.580
What?

21:02.550 --> 21:07.080
I said some harsh things to Akane-chan 
because I was so irritated.

21:07.680 --> 21:11.160
Apologize to her for me later, would you?

21:11.470 --> 21:14.460
No way. You gotta do that yourself.

21:15.290 --> 21:19.260
Why?! You're so mean!

21:20.420 --> 21:22.590
<b>Sexy Attack!</b>

21:20.750 --> 21:22.720
<i>Sexy Attack!</i>

21:22.720 --> 21:23.810
Hey!

21:25.620 --> 21:27.120
Sexy...

21:27.120 --> 21:28.460
Attack!

21:28.460 --> 21:30.050
Stop that!

23:27.090 --> 23:42.020
<b>Episode 9: "Riho and Her Past"</b>

23:27.090 --> 23:42.020
<b>Episode 9: "Riho and Her Past"</b>

23:27.620 --> 23:31.760
Everyone, thanks for coming to 
Mussy Mustache Girls' concert.

23:32.340 --> 23:34.180
We, Mussy Mustache Girls,

23:34.640 --> 23:36.260
want to play Mussy Mustache Girls music

23:36.780 --> 23:38.730
in a way that only Mussy Mustache Girls can,

23:39.230 --> 23:41.680
for those who support Mussy Mustache Girls—

23:39.690 --> 23:41.680
You just want to say that name, don't you?
